<title>GREECE: CONSTRUCTION FIRM ALTE SAYS H1 PROFIT UP 80 PCT.</title>
<headline>CONSTRUCTION FIRM ALTE SAYS H1 PROFIT UP 80 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek construction company Alte said its first half pretax profit rose 80 percent to 1.12 billion drachmas from 621 million drachmas in the same period a year ago.</p>
<p>Consolidated turnover jumped 100 percent to 4.0 billion drachmas and equity surged 135 percent to 11.6 billlion drachmas, it said.</p>
<p>Its orderbook of uncompleted projects stood at 50 billion drachmas on June 30, it added. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
